hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22687","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Amr, narrated to us, Khalid ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from his maternal aunt, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed while binding his finger from a scorpion sting, and said: You say there is no enemy, yet you will not cease fighting an enemy until there come Ya'juj and Ma'juj, broad faces, small eyes, reddish-white hair, pouring down from every elevation as if their faces are hammered shields."
"22688","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Rafi' ibn Salamah al-Ashja'i narrated to us, Hashraj ibn Ziyad al-Ashja'i narrated to me, from his grandmother, mother of his father, that she said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Khaybar, while I was the sixth of six women. Then it reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that women were with him, so he sent to us and said: What brought you out, and by whose command did you come out? So we said: We came out to hand arrows and give the people sawiq to drink, and with us is what we treat the wounded with, and we spin hair and help with it in the path of Allah. He said: Stand and turn back. Then when Allah opened Khaybar to him, he allotted for us shares like the shares of the man. I said: O grandmother, what did he allot for you? She said: Dates."
